    "bio": [
      "Dr. Bing Zhou is an Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) in the Department of Geography and Sustainability at the University of Tennessee, Knoxville. He leads the GRIND Lab (Geospatial Responsible AI for Nature-human Dynamics Laboratory).",
      "Dr. Zhou's research focuses on developing responsible geospatial AI to understand and mitigate coupled nature-human risks. His work spans GeoAI model design, remote sensing applications, and explainable AI for disaster detection, forecasting, and impact assessment across space and time.",
      "His work integrates remote sensing, street-view imagery, human mobility, environmental monitoring, and other geospatial big data to examine patterns of exposure, vulnerability, and recovery. Through GRIND Lab, he emphasizes responsible and interdisciplinary geospatial research that translates advanced AI methods into actionable knowledge for building more resilient, equitable, and healthy communities."
